  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "$\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0}(\\operatorname{cosec} x)^{1 / \\log x}$ is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "DmRka",
      "text": "0",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "tvfgZ",
      "text": "1",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "L0QJ0",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{e}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ybzpn",
      "text": "None of these",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $y=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0}(\\operatorname{cosec} x)^{1 / \\log x}$\r\n\r\nTaking $\\log$ on both sides, we get\r\n\r\n$\\log y=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{\\log \\operatorname{cosec} x}{\\log x}\\left[\\frac{\\infty}{\\infty}\\right.$ form $]$\r\n\r\n$=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{-\\cot x}{1 / x} \\quad$ (ByL' Hospital rule)\r\n\r\n$=-\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{x}{\\tan x} \\quad\\left(\\because \\cot x=\\frac{1}{\\tan x}\\right)$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\log y=-1$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow y=e^{-1}=\\frac{1}{e}$\r\n\r\nHence, required limit $=\\frac{1}{e}$",
    "image": null
  },
